  "reading": {
   "title": "The to-do list",
   "text": "It is Hafsa's first week at the front office. On Monday morning, Mr. Brown gives her a to-do list.\n\n\"Have you finished the attendance report yet?\" he asks. \"Not yet,\" Hafsa says. \"But I have already printed the forms, and I have just copied the new lunch menu.\" Mr. Brown nods. \"Good. The principal's meeting is at ten. Have you sent her the agenda yet?\" Hafsa checks her computer. \"Yes, I have. I sent it five minutes ago.\"\n\nThen the phone rings. A parent wants to talk to Ms. Carter. \"Ms. Carter hasn't come in yet,\" Hafsa says, \"but I can take a message.\" After the call, Mr. Brown smiles. \"You have done a lot this morning. The only task you haven't done yet is lunch!\" Hafsa laughs and writes the last item on her list: eat lunch.",
   "glossary": [
    {
     "en": "front office",
     "tr": "okulun ön ofisi"
    },
    {
     "en": "agenda",
     "tr": "gündem, toplantı programı"
    },
    {
     "en": "message",
     "tr": "mesaj, not"
    },
    {
     "en": "item",
     "tr": "madde"
    }
   ],
